</groundspeak:long_description><groundspeak:encoded_hints>padlock, window shutter</groundspeak:encoded_hints><groundspeak:logs><groundspeak:log id="1382284405"><groundspeak:date>2026-09-02T16:17:37</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Unknown</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="449640">Ogniz</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Gone. Will be replaced.</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1379628908"><groundspeak:date>2026-08-19T12:00:00</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Didn't find it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="7463513">ErwinKarin</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Wij zijn op reis met een groep van 29 geocachers uit Nederland en België om Oslo, Stockholm en Mariehamn te ontdekken. Tijdens deze trip geniet iedereen van de vrijheid om zijn eigen plan te trekken: geocachen, cultuur opsnuiven en de prachtige omgeving verkennen. Daarom gaat ieder op pad in kleine groepjes.

Wij, ErwinKarin, geocachen samen met Marcske57, Alwina0, KlimOpers en Zwarte-Panter en loggen onder de teamnaam VLNL.

Langs deze weg willen wij alle cache-eigenaren bedanken die deze mooie dagen en avonturen mogelijk hebben gemaakt. 

Dank voor het leggen en onderhouden van de cache!

Vi är på resa med en grupp på 29 geocachare från Nederländerna och Belgien för att upptäcka Oslo, Stockholm och Mariehamn. Här råder full frihet att göra precis det man vill: geocacha, ta del av kultur och njuta av den nya omgivningen. Därför ger sig alla ut i små grupper.

Vi, ErwinKarin, geocachar tillsammans med Marcske57, Alwina0, KlimOpers och Zwarte-Panter och loggar under teamnamnet VLNL.

Vi vill gärna tacka alla cacheägare som har gjort dessa härliga dagar möjliga. 

Tack för cachen!</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1373784412"><groundspeak:date>2026-07-20T12:00:00</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Didn't find it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="50726458">530414</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Fant ikke denne dessverre </groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1371116946"><groundspeak:date>2026-07-09T12:00:00</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="7769408">Team LP+MS</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Fundet på vores lille mini ferie</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1365536379"><groundspeak:date>2026-06-06T12:00:00</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="4713964">Sensa-5</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Schwedischer Nationalfeiertag in Schweden und wir waren bei den Feierlichkeiten vor dem königlichen Schloss hautnah dabei. Das war sehr beeindruckend. 
Aber nicht nur das wurde bestaunt, sondern auch Stockholm endeckt und dabei zahlreiche virtuelle Caches besucht und traditionelle sowie Mystery Caches gesucht. Einen Earthcache war auch dabei.
Unser Einheitslog möchten wir entschuldigen und soll in keinster Weise die Anerkennung der Mühen für die Hege und Pflege der Caches schmälern.
DfdC, Sensa-5

In einem Logbuch, ob groß ob klein, 
da muss auch unser Name rein.
Ob Vorne, Mitte, Hinten,
hier wird sich wohl ein Plätzchen finden.
So können wir auch weiter vorn im Logbuch stehen
und Du kannst unseren Eintrag nicht an letzter Stelle sehen.</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1161444469"><groundspeak:date>2023-04-22T12:00:00</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="24157615">mikkokalevi</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">En dagsvandring i Stockholm, med syfte att få olika typer av upptäckter, detta var en av dem.  tack för geocache.</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log></groundspeak:logs></groundspeak:cache></wpt><wpt lat="59.32261666666667" lon="18.073166666666665"><time>2007-01-09T00:00:00</time><name>GC109NX</name><desc>The Iron Family by Kire1 (adopted by herrFamaxe)</desc><url>https://www.geocaching.com/geocache/GC109NX</url><urlname>The Iron Family</urlname><sym>Geocache Found</sym><type>Geocache|Letterbox Hybrid</type><groundspeak:cache id="521729" available="true" archived="false"><groundspeak:name>The Iron Family</groundspeak:name><groundspeak:placed_by>Kire1 (adopted by herrFamaxe)</groundspeak:placed_by><groundspeak:owner id="18264693">herrFamaxe</groundspeak:owner><groundspeak:type>Letterbox Hybrid</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:container>Small</groundspeak:container><groundspeak:attributes><groundspeak:attribute id="41" inc="1">Stroller accessible</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="14" inc="1">Recommended at night</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="40" inc="1">Stealth required</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="15" inc="1">Available in winter</groundspeak:attribute></groundspeak:attributes><groundspeak:difficulty>3</groundspeak:difficulty><groundspeak:terrain>2</groundspeak:terrain><groundspeak:country>Sweden</groundspeak:country><groundspeak:state>Stockholm</groundspeak:state><groundspeak:short_description>
</groundspeak:short_description><groundspeak:long_description>This little story starts with an unhappy little boy. Your mission is to help him find his family and bring them home. You find him alone at the given coordinates in "Bollhustäppan" - the garden between "Bollhuset"/"The Finnish Church" and Trädgårdsgatan (close to Köpmangatan) in the beautiful Old Towm.
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="http://img.groundspeak.com/cache/bf57444f-94d2-4811-b15c-f8a986a8bba1.jpg" align="left" hspace="4" height="221" width="295" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;big&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Step 1: Find him, console him!&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/big&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Your first action is to console him. Please give the poor little Iron Boy some gift. People from all over the world come to pay him a visit and they leave him coins, toys, clothes etc in exchange for luck. He, perhaps the smallest statue in the world, just a palm high, sits quiet in his garden. Many people also rub his head for luck or wisdom. That's the reason of his shiny head! &lt;font color="red"&gt;&lt;b&gt;To complete the first step, please take and publish a photo of the Iron Boy with your gift&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;big&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Step 2: Find his Family!&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/big&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
The Iron family in despair is situated 340 meters from the Iron boy, in an angle of 221,7 degrees. Just like the Iron Boy, this is a rather unique statue, because it is movable! Please do some tranfers. Photos are ok, but not a condition for permission logging the box. Now the Iron Family is reunited - but unfortunately still far from home.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="http://img.groundspeak.com/cache/b8b3bcd8-b38b-446b-b34d-07dda3e38e11.jpg" align="right" hspace="4" height="273" width="205" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;big&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Step 3: Bring them home&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/big&gt; (figuratively speaking)&lt;br /&gt;
They live in a Market, a Square (in Swedish: "Torg") in the section of the city where you are, "Gamla stan" - you do not have to change district. The Market has got its name from the Familys name - the metal (in Swedish "Järn"). To get the place in the Square, where they live, please read the signs at the statue in step 2 (The Family) and translate the letters below:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color="red"&gt;AAAAAAAAAAAA&lt;br /&gt;
BBBB CCCC&lt;br /&gt;
DDD EEEEEEEE&lt;br /&gt;
F GGGG&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div align="center"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color="red"&gt;&lt;img src="http://img.groundspeak.com/cache/4a6983ca-2dcf-4125-9be0-0c0d90f3b99a.jpg" /&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color="red"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color="red"&gt;You find their home in the square/market at:&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color="red"&gt;E4A7 "C""O"B1E2B2E6&lt;br /&gt;
G3,C4 E8 A10D1&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;b&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/b&gt;
&lt;div align="center"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;img src="http://img.groundspeak.com/cache/61ea529e-26f5-4c0b-aee0-8f7bc9a3c2b8.jpg" /&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;b&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/b&gt;
&lt;div align="left"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color="blue"&gt;Please do not remove &lt;u&gt;&lt;big&gt;the stamp&lt;/big&gt;&lt;/u&gt; from the box! It belongs to The Iron Family!&lt;br /&gt;
Please draw a lot of attention to mugglers!!! Never ever trust them! (c; Therefore &lt;u&gt;please log the cache between 20:00 and 07:00&lt;/u&gt;.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

</groundspeak:long_description><groundspeak:encoded_hints /><groundspeak:logs><groundspeak:log id="1382206766"><groundspeak:date>2026-09-01T23:28:52</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="1557211">TZ Toy</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">I like clever hides and this hit on all cylinders. Interesting places, good story, clever puzzle and a tricky find (not so much to find, but to retrieve). Henny Penny figured out the location by dinner time. We located what we thought was the cache, but it was too early in the evening to grab it. Had a nice dinner and came back about 9:30. It wasn’t where we thought. Didn’t take too much more searching to find it, but as an early log pointed out “it was way inside”. Went back to our room. Fabricated a TOTT. And made the grab about 10:00. Fav for sure. TFTH </groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1382029140"><groundspeak:date>2026-08-31T12:00:00</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Didn't find it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="5458274">FionaCH</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">This cache came highly recommended to me - and I'm really glad we were able to do most of it. Loved the wee iron boy and we left an offering of a 2p coin! Sadly though, I couldn't get near enough to the final to retrieve due to many muggles - and I'm almost always in my bed during the suggested hours of finding! But not a wasted journey as not sure we would have visited the iron family otherwise. Thanks.</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1381437439"><groundspeak:date>2026-08-29T12:00:00</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="4520043">andrega</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">We found the final, but it is sooooo deep inside...

TFTC</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1381007855"><groundspeak:date>2026-08-24T12:00:00</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Write note</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="1858750">ronija</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Hello,
Sztokholmskie keszowanie na luzie, zgodnie ze szwedzką tradycją "fika" 🙂 Luz, zero pośpiechu, przyjemność na całego. Etapy odnalezione bez problemu, jednak moim zdaniem w finale nie było pojemnika z logbookiem 😟  Pzdr, Wojtek</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1380511066"><groundspeak:date>2026-08-23T12:00:00</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="2020538">f1nn</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">I had already solved the task at home, and when we passed by the final location on our walk through Gamla Stan this morning, we made a quick grab.

Together with butterfly-n25
Hälsningar från Österrike! 🇦🇹
TFTC f1nn</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1161444263"><groundspeak:date>2023-04-22T12:00:00</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="24157615">mikkokalevi</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">En dagsvandring i Stockholm, med syfte att få olika typer av upptäckter, detta var en av dem.  tack för geocache.</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log></groundspeak:logs></groundspeak:cache></wpt><wpt lat="59.3212666666667" lon="18.0743333333333"><time>2020-10-28T00:00:00</time><name>GC8W9D7</name><desc>Guldbron - The Golden bridge by Tompalin</desc><url>https://www.geocaching.com/geocache/GC8W9D7</url><urlname>Guldbron - The Golden bridge</urlname><sym>Geocache Found</sym><type>Geocache|Traditional Cache</type><groundspeak:cache id="7790464" available="true" archived="false"><groundspeak:name>Guldbron - The Golden bridge</groundspeak:name><groundspeak:placed_by>Tompalin</groundspeak:placed_by><groundspeak:owner id="6690876">Tompalin</groundspeak:owner><groundspeak:type>Traditional Cache</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:container>Micro</groundspeak:container><groundspeak:attributes><groundspeak:attribute id="24" inc="1">Wheelchair accessible</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="6" inc="1">Recommended for kids</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="41" inc="1">Stroller accessible</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="1" inc="1">Dogs</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="8" inc="1">Scenic view</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="13" inc="1">Available 24/7</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="7" inc="1">Takes less than one hour</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="32" inc="1">Bicycles</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="55" inc="1">Short hike (&lt;1 km)</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="63" inc="1">Recommended for tourists</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="26" inc="1">Public transportation nearby</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="15" inc="1">Available in winter</groundspeak:attribute></groundspeak:attributes><groundspeak:difficulty>1.5</groundspeak:difficulty><groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain><groundspeak:country>Sweden</groundspeak:country><groundspeak:state>Stockholm</groundspeak:state><groundspeak:short_description>
</groundspeak:short_description><groundspeak:long_description>&lt;h1&gt;Välkommen till Guldbron!&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Guldbron&lt;/strong&gt;, formellt &lt;em&gt;Slussbron&lt;span style="font-size:10.8333px;"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt; är huvudbron för vägtrafik samt gående och cyklister som förbinder &lt;a href="https://sv.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gamla_stan" title="Gamla stan"&gt;Gamla stan&lt;/a&gt; med &lt;a href="https://sv.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/S%C3%B6dermalm" title="Södermalm"&gt;Södermalm&lt;/a&gt; i centrala &lt;a href="https://sv.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stockholm" title="Stockholm"&gt;Stockholm&lt;/a&gt;. Bron, som är en del i &lt;a href="https://sv.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Projekt_Slussen" title="Projekt Slussen"&gt;Projekt Slussen&lt;/a&gt;, invigdes söndagen den 25 oktober 2020 och öppnades för trafik dagen därpå. På grund av sin färgsättning kallas den inofficiellt ofta &lt;em&gt;Guldbron&lt;/em&gt;. Livslängden beräknas till 120 år.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;BYOP!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;Welcome to The golden bridge!&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The golden bridge, formally Slussbron, is the main bridge for road traffic as well as pedestrians and cyclists who connect the Old Town with Södermalm in central Stockholm. The bridge, which is part of Project Slussen, was inaugurated on Sunday 25 October 2020 and opened for the following traffic days. Due to its color scheme, it is unofficially often called the Golden Bridge. Life expectancy is estimated at 120 years.&lt;/p&gt;
</groundspeak:long_description><groundspeak:encoded_hints>Spoiler picture
</groundspeak:encoded_hints><groundspeak:logs><groundspeak:log id="1382150200"><groundspeak:date>2026-09-01T18:01:49</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="44586689">sonjand</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Bei unserem Ausflug schnell gefunden </groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1382180930"><groundspeak:date>2026-09-01T12:00:00</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="3696982">DeLaTrick</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Angefangen hat alles im Baltikum und nun sind brisen60 und wir auch endlich in Schweden angekommen. So langsam geht es jetzt schon wieder in Richtung Heimat, doch vorher wollten wir der schönen Stadt Stockholm noch einen Besuch abstatten. Nach fünf Jahren sind wir nun mal wieder in der Hauptstadt und wir haben wieder jede Menge fantastische Eindrücke und Erinnerungen mitnehmen können
Dabei kam das Thema Cachen natürlich auch nicht zu kurz, denn damit kann man eine Statdbesichtigung wunderbar verbinden. Hier sind wir dann auch gewesen und haben uns der Aufgabe gestellt.
Vielen Dank dafür, beste Grüße und

--- T4TC ---

Allt började i Baltikum, och nu har brisen60 och vi äntligen anlänt till Sverige. Vi är på väg hemåt i lugn takt, men innan dess ville vi besöka den vackra staden Stockholm. Vi är tillbaka i huvudstaden efter fem år, och återigen har vi samlat på oss massor av fantastiska intryck och minnen.
Naturligtvis fick geocaching också vara med på ett hörn, då det passar utmärkt ihop med sightseeing. Vi besökte denna plats och tog oss an utmaningen.
Stort tack, vänliga hälsningar och

--- T4TC ---</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1382177442"><groundspeak:date>2026-09-01T12:00:00</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="6704036">brisen60</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">An unserem zweiten Tag in Schweden sind DeLaTrick und wir in Stockholm angekommen.
Heute ging es kreuz und quer durch die ganze City. Unterwegs haben wir viele Dosen und virtuelle Caches gefunden.

Vielen Dank an **Tompalin** fürs Legen und Pflegen.

**Besten Gruß - brisen60**</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1382084202"><groundspeak:date>2026-09-01T11:26:59</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Write note</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="50542852">Rotkivnilmuk</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Hittade med @lisakarolina88</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1382084063"><groundspeak:date>2026-09-01T11:26:07</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="50542852">Rotkivnilmuk</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Kul!</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1161444103"><groundspeak:date>2023-04-22T12:00:00</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="24157615">mikkokalevi</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">En dagsvandring i Stockholm, med syfte att få olika typer av upptäckter, detta var en av dem.  tack för geocache.</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log></groundspeak:logs></groundspeak:cache></wpt><wpt lat="59.333217" lon="18.073017"><time>2019-07-05T00:00:00</time><name>GC88ZK3</name><desc>The Stockholm Syndrome by T@bibito</desc><url>https://www.geocaching.com/geocache/GC88ZK3</url><urlname>The Stockholm Syndrome</urlname><sym>Geocache Found</sym><type>Geocache|Virtual Cache</type><groundspeak:cache id="7244798" available="true" archived="false"><groundspeak:name>The Stockholm Syndrome</groundspeak:name><groundspeak:placed_by>T@bibito</groundspeak:placed_by><groundspeak:owner id="2099094">T@bibito</groundspeak:owner><groundspeak:type>Virtual Cache</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container><groundspeak:attributes><groundspeak:attribute id="24" inc="1">Wheelchair accessible</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="6" inc="1">Recommended for kids</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="1" inc="1">Dogs</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="13" inc="1">Available 24/7</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="7" inc="1">Takes less than one hour</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="63" inc="1">Recommended for tourists</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="59" inc="1">Food nearby</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="26" inc="1">Public transportation nearby</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="15" inc="1">Available in winter</groundspeak:attribute></groundspeak:attributes><groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty><groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain><groundspeak:country>Sweden</groundspeak:country><groundspeak:state>Stockholm</groundspeak:state><groundspeak:short_description>
</groundspeak:short_description><groundspeak:long_description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SWE - Stockholmssyndromet&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stockholmssyndromet, en term myntad av psykolog och kriminolog Nils Bejerot efter det berömda Norrmalmstorgsdramat som skedde i och omkring Kreditbanken mellan den 23-28 Augusti 1973 på Norrmalmstorg i Stockholm. Den ökände svenska bankrånaren Clark Olofsson höll, efter en misslyckat rånförsök, stora delar av bankpersonal gisslan under 5 dagar. Under tiden var det flera i gisslans som började fatta tycke för sin gisslantagare och som i slutändan till och med samarbetade för gisslantagarens syften. Detta psykologiska fenomen fick namnet Stockholmssyndromet och har sedan dess blivit den vedertagna begreppet i hela världen för dessa typer av extrema situationer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Det finns fyra stycken beståndsdelar som karaktäriserar Stockholmssyndromet;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Att gisslan utvecklar positiva känslor för sin gisslantagare.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Att gisslan och gisslantagare inte har någon tidigare relation, de känner inte varandra.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Att gisslan utvecklar en tveksamhet, till och med vägran, för att samarbeta med polisen eller annan myndighetspersonal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Att gisslan väljer att se sin gisslantagares mänskliga sidor, man identifierar sig, vilket också förmildrar hotbilden som hen utsätter gisslan för.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Det finns flera kända fall av Stockholmssyndromet genom historien. Det kanske mest kända gäller den amerikanska publicistdottern &lt;em&gt;Patty Hearst&lt;/em&gt; som vid 17 års ålder kidnappades från sitt hem i Berkley för att senare hjälpa sina kidnappare med både bankrån och utpressning. I den mer nutida fiktionen nämns &lt;em&gt;Belle&lt;/em&gt; i Disneys &lt;em&gt;Skönheten &amp;amp; Odjuret&lt;/em&gt; som ett utmärkt exempel på Stockholmssyndromet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:8px;"&gt;Källa; Wikipedia &amp;amp; diverse andra publika hemsidor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;UPPGIFT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Vid koordinaterna står du mitt på Norrmalmstorg, i närheten av där Kreditbanken tidigare låg. Ta ett kort på dig, och din GPS, där man tydligt ser dig själv samt Linderoths kalenderur som återfinns på fasaden på Kreditbankens tidigare kontor. Loggar som inte uppfyller dessa kriterier...&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ENG - The Stockholm syndrome&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Stockholm Syndrome, a term created by psychologist and criminologist Nils Bejerot after a hostage situation at the Kreditbanken bank in Stockholm in August 1973. The infamous Swedish bank robber Clark Olofsson took a group of bank employees hostage, for 5 days, after a failed robbery attempt. During the course of the hostage situation, parts of the hostages began to developed a bond with their captor to an extent they started supporting his cause. This psychological term got the name Stockholm syndrome and has, ever since, been a world-spread term describing this type of extreme situation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There are four key components that characterize Stockholm syndrome:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A hostage's development of positive feelings towards the captor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;No previous relationship between hostage and captor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A refusal by hostages to cooperate with police forces and other government authorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A hostage's belief in the humanity of the captor because they cease to perceive the captor as a threat when the victim holds the same values as the aggressor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There are several famous examples of the Stockholm syndrome. The most famous case might be that of &lt;em&gt;Patty Hearst&lt;/em&gt; who was abducted from here Berkeley home at the age of 17. Patty later joined the kidnappers' cause and assisted them both in robberies and blackmail. In recent fiction &lt;em&gt;Belle&lt;/em&gt;, from Disney's &lt;em&gt;Beauty and the Beast&lt;/em&gt;, is mentioned as a perfect example of Stockholm syndrome.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:8px;"&gt;&lt;em&gt;Source; Wikipedia &amp;amp; other public homepages&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TASK&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The posted coordinates will take you to the center of the square Norrmalmstorg. This is where the hostage situation took place at the former headquarters of Kreditbanken bank. On the facade of the former office there is a big public clock. Take a picture with you, and your gps, with a clear view of the clock in the background. Post the picture with your log. Logs that does not fulfill the requirments will....&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;h4&gt; &lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Virtual Rewards 2.0 - 2019/2020&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This Virtual Cache is part of a limited release of Virtuals created between June 4, 2019 and June 4, 2020. Only 4,000 cache owners were given the opportunity to hide a Virtual Cache. Learn more about Virtual Rewards 2.0 on the &lt;a href="https://www.geocaching.com/blog/2019/05/introducing-virtual-rewards-2-0/"&gt;Geocaching Blog&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

</groundspeak:long_description><groundspeak:encoded_hints /><groundspeak:logs><groundspeak:log id="1382094296"><groundspeak:date>2026-09-01T12:00:00</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="47809071">GoldFuchs1</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Tack</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1381902208"><groundspeak:date>2026-08-31T12:00:00</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="41446885">Chrisma80</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">On our way  to the airport... Thanks for the information and the cache!</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1381674829"><groundspeak:date>2026-08-30T12:04:51</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="5660998">janjorjack</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">An interesting story here. Great idea for a virtual.  Fav for me. Jtee and I are off on a grand adventure.  This time we are off to Sweden and the Aland Islands. It’s a new location for me so I am enjoying the sites and meeting new people too. Thanks for the smile.</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1381913112"><groundspeak:date>2026-08-30T12:04:10</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="164089">jtee</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">We're having a great time caching around the area..we had to stop for this one..thks for the fun </groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1381444333"><groundspeak:date>2026-08-29T12:48:41</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="5137813">MonsTTer</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Tftc🫡</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1118672274"><groundspeak:date>2022-08-14T12:00:00</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="24157615">mikkokalevi</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Terveiset Suomesta! Tack för geocache</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log></groundspeak:logs></groundspeak:cache></wpt><wpt lat="59.337017" lon="18.064"><time>2009-04-22T00:00:00</time><name>GC1Q4R4</name><desc>Brunkebergsåsen by herrFamaxe</desc><url>https://www.geocaching.com/geocache/GC1Q4R4</url><urlname>Brunkebergsåsen</urlname><sym>Geocache Found</sym><type>Geocache|Traditional Cache</type><groundspeak:cache id="1202186" available="true" archived="false"><groundspeak:name>Brunkebergsåsen</groundspeak:name><groundspeak:placed_by>herrFamaxe</groundspeak:placed_by><groundspeak:owner id="18264693">herrFamaxe</groundspeak:owner><groundspeak:type>Traditional Cache</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:container>Micro</groundspeak:container><groundspeak:attributes><groundspeak:attribute id="6" inc="1">Recommended for kids</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="41" inc="1">Stroller accessible</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="1" inc="1">Dogs</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="7" inc="1">Takes less than one hour</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="40" inc="1">Stealth required</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="15" inc="1">Available in winter</groundspeak:attribute></groundspeak:attributes><groundspeak:difficulty>2</groundspeak:difficulty><groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain><groundspeak:country>Sweden</groundspeak:country><groundspeak:state>Stockholm</groundspeak:state><groundspeak:short_description>
</groundspeak:short_description><groundspeak:long_description>&lt;img src="http://img.geocaching.com/cache/42b0c909-5a19-4b63-b32e-f5d30c472d79.jpg" alt="Brunkebergstunneln" border="0" align="top" /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
Sattelitmottagningen blir sämre och sämre ju närmare du kommer.&lt;br /&gt;
Satellite reception becomes worse and worse the closer you come.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;b&gt;Brunkebergsåsen, [SWE]&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Brunkebergsåsen är en rullstensås som hör ihop med Stockholmsåsen, den bildades för cirka 10 000 år sedan när den senaste inlandsisen smälte. Åsen har genom åren grävts bort mer och mer, Brunkebergstorg ligger nu 20 meter lägre än ursprungsåsen, både Kungsgatan och Hamngatan är grävda genom åsen. Södra delen av åsen är sedan länge bortfraktad. En stor del av massorna från åsen har använts för att fylla ut Klara sjö och Barnhusviken.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
Brunkebergstunneln byggdes mellan 1884 och 1886 under ledning av Knut Lindmark, den invigdes den 9 juni 1886 av kung Oskar II. Tunneln är 231 meter lång, 4 meter bred och nästan 4 meter hög. Knut Lindmark byggde även Katarinahissen. När hissen var en stor framgång för Knut Lindmark så blev tunneln en ekonomisk katastrof.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
Utanför Brunkebergstunnel, i korsningen Sveavägen - Tunnelgatan, blev Sveriges stadsminister Olof Palme mördad den 28 februari 1986.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
Tidigare låg cachen &lt;a href="http://www.geocaching.com/seek/cache_details.aspx?guid=6c9e81dd-9b2f-43d9-bcf1-4c38570f6852"&gt;The Murder Weapon&lt;/a&gt;, (av ulge02) här, den är arkiverad sen en tid tillbaka. Platsen är för bra för att det inte ska finnas en cache här. Jag hittade aldrig den tidigade cachen så jag vet inte om denna ligger på samma ställe.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;b&gt;Brunkebergsåsen, [ENG]&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Brunkeberg ridge is an esker linked to Stockholm ridge, it was formed about 10 000 years ago when the last glacier melted. The ridge has over the years been carved out more and more, Brunkebergstorg is now 20 meters lower than the original ridge, both Kungsgatan and Hamngatan is dug through the ridge. Southern part of the ridge is since long moved away. A large part of the masses from the ridge has been used to fill Klara sjö and Barnhusviken.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
Brunkebergstunnel was built between 1884 and 1886 under the leadership of Knut Lindmark, it was inaugurated June 9, 1886 by King Oskar II. The tunnel is 231 meters long, 4 meters wide and almost 4 meter tall. Knut Lindmark also built Katarina elevator. When the lift was a great success for Knut Lindmark, the tunnel became an economic disaster.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
Outside Brunkeberg Tunnel, at the junction Sveavägen - Tunnelgatan, the Swedish Prime Minister Olof Palme was murdered in February 28, 1986.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
Earlier the cache &lt;a href="http://www.geocaching.com/seek/cache_details.aspx?guid=6c9e81dd-9b2f-43d9-bcf1-4c38570f6852"&gt;The Murder Weapon&lt;/a&gt;, (by ulge02) was placed here, it is now archived for some time. This place is too good to not host a cache. I never found the earlier cache so I do not know if this is in the same place.
</groundspeak:long_description><groundspeak:encoded_hints>Lågt. Höger sida på spolier bilden, cachen syns.
Low. Right side in the spolier picture, the cache is visible.
