</groundspeak:short_description><groundspeak:long_description>&lt;p&gt;Welcome to Mynttorget - The Coin Square!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;From here you can see the Swedish Parliament Building right across the bridge, and the Royal Caste. In order to log this cache you should post a picture of yourself and/or your GPS from somewhere at Mynttorget, and at least one coin of any type. Include what kind of coin and currency is featured in the picture in your log. &lt;em&gt;You do not need to send me a DM&lt;/em&gt; (please don't, I'm getting spammed), just include picture and coin description in the ordinary log. Welcome and Good Luck!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;em&gt;Virtual Rewards 2.0 - 2019/2020&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This Virtual Cache is part of a limited release of Virtuals created between June 4, 2019 and June 4, 2020. Only 4,000 cache owners were given the opportunity to hide a Virtual Cache. Learn more about Virtual Rewards 2.0 on the &lt;a href="https://www.geocaching.com/blog/2019/05/introducing-virtual-rewards-2-0/"&gt;Geocaching Blog&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

</groundspeak:long_description><groundspeak:encoded_hints /><groundspeak:logs><groundspeak:log id="1382286298"><groundspeak:date>2026-09-02T12:00:00</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="47809071">GoldFuchs1</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Thank you for the cache. Greetings from Germany.</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1382282866"><groundspeak:date>2026-09-02T09:45:32</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="1557211">TZ Toy</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Henny Penny and I were out another day exploring Stockholm and came across another fun virtual. TFTH </groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1382112169"><groundspeak:date>2026-09-01T14:39:53</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="3566144">globo65</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">TFTC. The coin is a 5 Swiss Frank coin. On one side of the coin you see William Tell, a famous Swiss hero ...</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1382180239"><groundspeak:date>2026-09-01T12:00:00</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="3696982">DeLaTrick</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Angefangen hat alles im Baltikum und nun sind brisen60 und wir auch endlich in Schweden angekommen. So langsam geht es jetzt schon wieder in Richtung Heimat, doch vorher wollten wir der schönen Stadt Stockholm noch einen Besuch abstatten. Nach fünf Jahren sind wir nun mal wieder in der Hauptstadt und wir haben wieder jede Menge fantastische Eindrücke und Erinnerungen mitnehmen können
Dabei kam das Thema Cachen natürlich auch nicht zu kurz, denn damit kann man eine Statdbesichtigung wunderbar verbinden. Hier sind wir dann auch gewesen und haben uns der Aufgabe gestellt.
Vielen Dank dafür, beste Grüße und

--- T4TC ---

Allt började i Baltikum, och nu har brisen60 och vi äntligen anlänt till Sverige. Vi är på väg hemåt i lugn takt, men innan dess ville vi besöka den vackra staden Stockholm. Vi är tillbaka i huvudstaden efter fem år, och återigen har vi samlat på oss massor av fantastiska intryck och minnen.
Naturligtvis fick geocaching också vara med på ett hörn, då det passar utmärkt ihop med sightseeing. Vi besökte denna plats och tog oss an utmaningen.
Stort tack, vänliga hälsningar och

--- T4TC ---</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1382174649"><groundspeak:date>2026-09-01T12:00:00</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="6704036">brisen60</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">An unserem zweiten Tag in Schweden sind DeLaTrick und wir in Stockholm angekommen.
Heute ging es kreuz und quer durch die ganze City. Unterwegs haben wir viele Dosen und virtuelle Caches gefunden.

Vielen Dank an **Klossist: T** fürs Legen und Pflegen.

**Besten Gruß - brisen60**</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1118671803"><groundspeak:date>2022-08-14T12:00:00</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="24157615">mikkokalevi</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Terveiset Suomesta! Tack för geocache</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log></groundspeak:logs></groundspeak:cache></wpt><wpt lat="59.32705" lon="18.069217"><time>2008-06-18T00:00:00</time><name>GC1DBG5</name><desc>OTTT #2 – Changing of the Guard by Trang</desc><url>https://www.geocaching.com/geocache/GC1DBG5</url><urlname>OTTT #2 – Changing of the Guard</urlname><sym>Geocache Found</sym><type>Geocache|Traditional Cache</type><groundspeak:cache id="910756" available="true" archived="false"><groundspeak:name>OTTT #2 – Changing of the Guard</groundspeak:name><groundspeak:placed_by>Trang</groundspeak:placed_by><groundspeak:owner id="886479">Trang</groundspeak:owner><groundspeak:type>Traditional Cache</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:container>Other</groundspeak:container><groundspeak:attributes><groundspeak:attribute id="24" inc="1">Wheelchair accessible</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="13" inc="1">Available 24/7</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="7" inc="1">Takes less than one hour</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="40" inc="1">Stealth required</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="26" inc="1">Public transportation nearby</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="15" inc="1">Available in winter</groundspeak:attribute></groundspeak:attributes><groundspeak:difficulty>2</groundspeak:difficulty><groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain><groundspeak:country>Sweden</groundspeak:country><groundspeak:state>Stockholm</groundspeak:state><groundspeak:short_description>
</groundspeak:short_description><groundspeak:long_description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Swedens most logged cache – easy to find, quick to log, different from the rest.&lt;br /&gt;
Sveriges mest loggade cache – lätt att hitta, snabb att logga, inte som alla andra.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="http://img.geocaching.com/cache/39fecc9b-7c20-48df-8a86-e3be3efe2e86.jpg" /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;i&gt;Usually when &lt;b style="color:black;background-color:#ffff66;"&gt;geocaching&lt;/b&gt;, you get to see new and interesting places you probably would not have seen otherwise, and that is one of the great things about this hobby. But what if you are short of time when visiting a new town, and want to see the main tourist attractions and do some &lt;b style="color:black;background-color:#ffff66;"&gt;geocaching&lt;/b&gt; as well?&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;i&gt;In Stockholm the &lt;b&gt;On The Tourist Trail&lt;/b&gt; (OTTT) – series of caches could be the answer. These seven caches (plus one bonus mystery) are all hidden next to main tourist attractions, all on the Top-ten list of most visited places in town. Most of the OTTT-caches are easy to find and quick to log.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;i&gt;The caches are: &lt;a href="http://www.geocaching.com/seek/cache_details.aspx?guid=b1629f16-9f46-49c0-84f9-585d8dbb9b27"&gt;&lt;b&gt;OTTT #1&lt;/b&gt; – City Hall&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="http://www.geocaching.com/seek/cache_details.aspx?guid=611b097b-e43c-46ee-aae0-32c5b837f720"&gt;&lt;b&gt;OTTT #2&lt;/b&gt; – Changing of the Guard&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="http://www.geocaching.com/seek/cache_details.aspx?guid=ceedb2d1-e325-4d00-8125-baefed5f6792"&gt;&lt;b&gt;OTTT #3&lt;/b&gt; – Sightseeing&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="http://www.geocaching.com/seek/cache_details.aspx?guid=891e3d60-a783-4f92-8a4e-ae3f306fcaa3"&gt;&lt;b&gt;OTTT #4&lt;/b&gt; – Museum of Modern Art&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="http://www.geocaching.com/seek/cache_details.aspx?guid=1d8f6fe3-9062-4c69-8c73-b5fa16009ce5"&gt;&lt;b&gt;OTTT #5&lt;/b&gt; – Vasa&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="http://www.geocaching.com/seek/cache_details.aspx?guid=23afd7aa-066a-44b2-ada2-43f3f0c85d22"&gt;&lt;b&gt;OTTT #6&lt;/b&gt; – Skansen&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/i&gt;, &lt;i&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.geocaching.com/seek/cache_details.aspx?guid=2b8b0a96-c3cf-417c-85d6-8c162c43ec5f"&gt;&lt;b&gt;OTTT #7&lt;/b&gt; – Fjällgatan&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;and the bonus mystery&lt;/i&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.geocaching.com/seek/cache_details.aspx?guid=8cdc612a-0248-4bce-a6d8-71f209770087"&gt;&lt;b&gt;OTTT #8&lt;/b&gt; – Bulls Eye&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/i&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;img src="http://img.geocaching.com/cache/3d459387-cc3c-4731-a0fc-b08251728e17.jpg" /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;font size="+1"&gt;The most logged cache in Sweden!&lt;br /&gt;
Now more than &lt;font size="+2"&gt;22.000&lt;/font&gt; found logs!&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="+1"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font size="+2"&gt;Changing of the Guard&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The changing of the guard at the Royal Palace takes place at the outer courtyard each day, during the summer months, at 12.15 (13.15 on Sundays). During the winter season a smaller cermony is held at the courtyard every Wednesday, Saturday and Sunday. From the cache the shortest way to the outer courtyard is to walk across the street and then take the stairs (for the moment renovation work going on and the stairs are sealed of - follow Västerlånggatan, and at the first intersection, walk to the left). For more information, please visit: &lt;a href="https://www.forsvarsmakten.se/sv/var-verksamhet/publik-verksamhet/hogvakten/tid-och-plats-for-hogvakten/" target="_blank"&gt;Högvakten&lt;/a&gt; (in English: &lt;a href="https://www.forsvarsmakten.se/en/activities/events/the-royal-guards/changing-of-the-guard/" target="_blank"&gt;The Royal Guards&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
When searching for, and logging this cache, be &lt;b&gt;extremely stealthy&lt;/b&gt;, the place is busy and there are always lots of mugglers around. After logging, please be sure to put the cache back exactly as found, thanks.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

</groundspeak:long_description><groundspeak:encoded_hints>[Swe:] Lyktstolpe
[Eng:] Lamppost</groundspeak:encoded_hints><groundspeak:logs><groundspeak:log id="1382290200"><groundspeak:date>2026-09-02T12:00:00</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="47809071">GoldFuchs1</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Thanks for the cache. Greetings from Germany.</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1382231157"><groundspeak:date>2026-09-02T09:51:08</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="1557211">TZ Toy</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Another quick find for me and Henny Penny as we explore Stockholm. TFTH </groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1382133956"><groundspeak:date>2026-09-01T16:38:01</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="54387766">joshandamelie</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">beautiful location

find #75 - TFTC</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1382130794"><groundspeak:date>2026-09-01T16:20:47</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="43779112">ZsembesVombat</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Kosz a rejtest
</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1382121870"><groundspeak:date>2026-09-01T15:31:36</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="44586689">sonjand</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Wonderful city - Thank you</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1118671676"><groundspeak:date>2022-08-14T12:00:00</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="24157615">mikkokalevi</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Terveiset Suomesta! Tack för geocache</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log></groundspeak:logs></groundspeak:cache></wpt><wpt lat="59.326417" lon="18.070317"><time>2020-06-13T00:00:00</time><name>GC88ZDZ</name><desc>The Royal Palace by Anden81</desc><url>https://www.geocaching.com/geocache/GC88ZDZ</url><urlname>The Royal Palace</urlname><sym>Geocache Found</sym><type>Geocache|Virtual Cache</type><groundspeak:cache id="7244639" available="true" archived="false"><groundspeak:name>The Royal Palace</groundspeak:name><groundspeak:placed_by>Anden81</groundspeak:placed_by><groundspeak:owner id="1696778">Anden81</groundspeak:owner><groundspeak:type>Virtual Cache</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container><groundspeak:attributes><groundspeak:attribute id="24" inc="1">Wheelchair accessible</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="6" inc="1">Recommended for kids</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="41" inc="1">Stroller accessible</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="63" inc="1">Recommended for tourists</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="26" inc="1">Public transportation nearby</groundspeak:attribute></groundspeak:attributes><groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty><groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain><groundspeak:country>Sweden</groundspeak:country><groundspeak:state>Stockholm</groundspeak:state><groundspeak:short_description>
</groundspeak:short_description><groundspeak:long_description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt src="https://s3.amazonaws.com/gs-geo-images/5d10c0eb-84d5-4203-b9f6-3716fa62f737.jpg" style="height:263px;width:350px;" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Welcome to one of the largest palaces in Europe! The Royal Palace is the official residence of His Majesty the King of Sweden, with over 600 rooms.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
The Palace is open to the public and offers no less than five museums. The Palace was largely built during the eighteenth century in the Italian Baroque style, on the spot where the “Tre Kronor” castle burned down in 1697. Visit the reception rooms with splendid interiors from the eighteenth and nineteenth centuries, Rikssalen (the Hall of State) with Queen Kristina’s silver throne, and Ordenssalarna (Halls of the Orders of Chivalry). You can also see Gustav III’s Museum of Antiquities, the Tre Kronor Museum, and the Treasury.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Royal Palace also contains the Armory, with royal costumes and armor, as well as coronation carriages and magnificent coaches from the Royal Stable. Make sure not to miss the parade of soldiers and the daily changing of the guard.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Source: &lt;a href="https://www.visitstockholm.com/"&gt;Visit Stockholm&lt;/a&gt; where you can find a lot of other places to visit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To log this cache&lt;/strong&gt; just go to the posted coordinates and take a photo of you or a part of you with at least one cannon included in the picture and post it with your log. (The face doesn't have to be visible).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Virtual Rewards 2.0 - 2019/2020&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This Virtual Cache is part of a limited release of Virtuals created between June 4, 2019 and June 4, 2020. Only 4,000 cache owners were given the opportunity to hide a Virtual Cache. Learn more about Virtual Rewards 2.0 on the &lt;a href="https://www.geocaching.com/blog/2019/05/introducing-virtual-rewards-2-0/"&gt;Geocaching Blog&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

</groundspeak:long_description><groundspeak:encoded_hints /><groundspeak:logs><groundspeak:log id="1382238246"><groundspeak:date>2026-09-02T12:00:00</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="47809071">GoldFuchs1</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Tack</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1382162789"><groundspeak:date>2026-09-01T19:05:42</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="1557211">TZ Toy</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Henny Penny and I went past this side of the palace after a day of exploring day 2 of Stockholm. Not near as busy in the square as when the cruise ships area in town. TFTH </groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1382103992"><groundspeak:date>2026-09-01T13:49:34</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="44586689">sonjand</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Thank you </groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1382174534"><groundspeak:date>2026-09-01T12:00:00</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="6704036">brisen60</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">An unserem zweiten Tag in Schweden sind DeLaTrick und wir in Stockholm angekommen.
Heute ging es kreuz und quer durch die ganze City. Unterwegs haben wir viele Dosen und virtuelle Caches gefunden.

Vielen Dank an **Anden81** fürs Legen und Pflegen.

**Besten Gruß - brisen60**</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1382060116"><groundspeak:date>2026-08-31T12:00:00</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="2034679">Aljonis</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Thanks for showing us this place. 
♥️lichen Dank fürs Herlocken an Anden81
Sonnige Grüße Aljonis 🍀</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1118671536"><groundspeak:date>2022-08-14T12:00:00</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="24157615">mikkokalevi</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Terveiset Suomesta! Tack för geocache</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log></groundspeak:logs></groundspeak:cache></wpt><wpt lat="59.32465" lon="18.069733"><time>2007-05-13T00:00:00</time><name>GC12WJT</name><desc>Urban Birdhouse by Bo &amp; Elisabeth</desc><url>https://www.geocaching.com/geocache/GC12WJT</url><urlname>Urban Birdhouse</urlname><sym>Geocache Found</sym><type>Geocache|Traditional Cache</type><groundspeak:cache id="598513" available="false" archived="true"><groundspeak:name>Urban Birdhouse</groundspeak:name><groundspeak:placed_by>Bo &amp; Elisabeth</groundspeak:placed_by><groundspeak:owner id="61878">Elritsa</groundspeak:owner><groundspeak:type>Traditional Cache</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:container>Micro</groundspeak:container><groundspeak:attributes /><groundspeak:difficulty>2</groundspeak:difficulty><groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain><groundspeak:country>Sweden</groundspeak:country><groundspeak:state>Stockholm</groundspeak:state><groundspeak:short_description /><groundspeak:long_description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=
"http://img.geocaching.com/cache/0cde2d07-d802-4fd4-b982-2b92083e4898.jpg"
width="365" height="210" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face="Comic Sans MS"&gt;En ganska enkel mikro p&amp;aring; en
plats med massor av mugglare. Penna saknas i burken !&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;font color="#990000" face="Comic Sans MS"&gt;A rather simple micro
in a place with lots of muggles around. Bring your own pen
!&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font face="Comic Sans MS"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description><groundspeak:encoded_hints>magnetic</groundspeak:encoded_hints><groundspeak:logs><groundspeak:log id="1350835265"><groundspeak:date>2026-03-09T20:54:00</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Didn't find it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="2823864">joom</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false"> @20:54

Five days, the same number of fingers on a hand, with my beloved H., spent on a holiday in Stockholm, the Venice of the North.
Second day, the one that I walked the most: around 30 kilometres.
Evening walk after dinner towards this [event](https://coord.info/GCBHK4J) with a rather late hour for these latitudes but that surprisingly had more attendees than expected.

Unfortunately, the cache is gone. We searched for the cache twice. In the morning on the way to the [Gamla Stan](https://coord.info/GC3ANAG) wherigo. At the first I noticed that something wrong happened. The birdhouse is nowhere to be seen. As sometimes caches change I though that somehow another cache, a nano or a micro, was there.
On a second time, with less people around, I quickly understood that nothing was there to be found.
It was later at the evening that we discovered that the cache was archived since the signal, and birdhouse, were removal.

Tack för cachen.
Hälsningar från Portugal.

</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1348310630"><groundspeak:date>2026-03-09T19:27:27</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Archived</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="61878">Elritsa</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Idag åkte jag till Stockholm för att byta loggbok i cachen. Döm om min förvåning när jag insåg att cachen, ja hela gömstället var borta!
Gatukontoret har tydligen varit där och monterat ner vägskylten som satt på husväggen och då försvann både fågelholken och gömstället.
Cachen blev 19 år och fick över 20 000 Found-loggar men nu är det slut. Snyft.
/Bosse</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1348132500"><groundspeak:date>2026-03-08T19:25:59</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Didn't find it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="51347369">icemanceuta</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">No ha habido suerte...</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1346266223"><groundspeak:date>2026-02-25T12:00:00</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="3307523">Luk&amp;Ria</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Treinreis door Scandinavië.
Dag 5, stad 3: Stockholm.

Urban Birdhouse: in 2019 niets gevonden, maar nu hebben we meer geluk.

TFTC, Bo &amp; Elisabeth.
Vondst #10798 om 10:25 🇧🇪</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1346058956"><groundspeak:date>2026-02-23T07:39:16</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="33035026">Kerttuterttu</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">😊</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1118671419"><groundspeak:date>2022-08-14T12:00:00</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="24157615">mikkokalevi</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Terveiset Suomesta! Tack för geocache</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log></groundspeak:logs></groundspeak:cache></wpt><wpt lat="59.324783" lon="18.070567"><time>2018-08-24T00:00:00</time><name>GC7B86A</name><desc>Stortorget by JoRos</desc><url>https://www.geocaching.com/geocache/GC7B86A</url><urlname>Stortorget</urlname><sym>Geocache Found</sym><type>Geocache|Virtual Cache</type><groundspeak:cache id="6389112" available="true" archived="false"><groundspeak:name>Stortorget</groundspeak:name><groundspeak:placed_by>JoRos</groundspeak:placed_by><groundspeak:owner id="3785207">JoRos</groundspeak:owner><groundspeak:type>Virtual Cache</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container><groundspeak:attributes><groundspeak:attribute id="24" inc="1">Wheelchair accessible</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="6" inc="1">Recommended for kids</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="41" inc="1">Stroller accessible</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="13" inc="1">Available 24/7</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="63" inc="1">Recommended for tourists</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="59" inc="1">Food nearby</groundspeak:attribute></groundspeak:attributes><groundspeak:difficulty>1.5</groundspeak:difficulty><groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain><groundspeak:country>Sweden</groundspeak:country><groundspeak:state>Stockholm</groundspeak:state><groundspeak:short_description>
</groundspeak:short_description><groundspeak:long_description>&lt;p dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:16pt;font-family:Cambria;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;"&gt;Stortorget ’’The Big Square’&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:12pt;font-family:Cambria;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;"&gt;This is the city’s oldest square, it was here when Stockholm was founded somewhere between year 1187 and 1252.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:16pt;font-family:Cambria;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;"&gt;The square’s history&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt src="https://img.geocaching.com/cache/large/ec751ba6-6ecf-42a2-b368-e6cd18927fc2.jpg" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:12pt;font-family:Cambria;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;"&gt;The Big Square is Stockholm’s oldest square; it came to when the conurbation started at the top of Stadsholmen sometime between 1187 and 1252. The map above is from the year 1547 (the oldest map of Stockholm).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"&gt;
&lt;li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type:decimal;font-size:12pt;font-family:Cambria;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;"&gt;
&lt;p dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:12pt;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;"&gt;The Big Square with red color&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type:decimal;font-size:12pt;font-family:Cambria;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;"&gt;
&lt;p dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:12pt;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;"&gt;Town Hall&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type:decimal;font-size:12pt;font-family:Cambria;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;"&gt;
&lt;p dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:12pt;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;"&gt;The Big Church&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type:decimal;font-size:12pt;font-family:Cambria;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;"&gt;
&lt;p dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:12pt;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;"&gt;The Castle ‘’Tre Kronor’’&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type:decimal;font-size:12pt;font-family:Cambria;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;"&gt;
&lt;p dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:12pt;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;"&gt;Köpmangatan&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type:decimal;font-size:12pt;font-family:Cambria;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;"&gt;
&lt;p dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:12pt;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;"&gt;Köpmanporten (a gate)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type:decimal;font-size:12pt;font-family:Cambria;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;"&gt;
&lt;p dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:12pt;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;"&gt;Svartmangatan&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type:decimal;font-size:12pt;font-family:Cambria;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;"&gt;
&lt;p dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:12pt;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;"&gt;Skomakargatan&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
 &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:12pt;font-family:Cambria;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;"&gt;The Big Square is in the same spot and almost the same size as it was in the Middle Ages, it has changed very little since.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:12pt;font-family:Cambria;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;"&gt;During the Middle Ages and until year 1523 The Big Square was the most important square in the city for most things, they had a marketplace and the council hall where they also kept people who were arrested and waited on their sentence. It also had the town’s most important wells and was the place where only the most powerful and rich could afford to live.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:12pt;font-family:Cambria;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;"&gt;​&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt src="https://img.geocaching.com/cache/large/60aab868-a6b1-45dd-b506-4099d1db07f9.jpg" style="width:500px;height:349px;" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Cambria;font-size:12pt;white-space:pre-wrap;"&gt;The picture above shows an example how it could look a normal day at the square during the Middle Age. (Picture from Stockholm’s art show 1897.)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:12pt;font-family:Cambria;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;"&gt;As the city grew the square got less important as a marketplace and after 1849 only dairy products were allowed to be sold here. Today the only thing left of the marketplace is the annual Christmas market that takes place for a few weeks before Christmas.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:12pt;font-family:Cambria;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;"&gt;The year of 1520 occurred something that today is known as Stockholms blodbad (blood bath). It was the union king Kristian II that had 92 people executed, most of them beheaded on this square. But it was not the first occasion of executions; the first documented time in the books was the year 1280 when king Magnus Ladulås had rioters killed, Jöns Karlsson, Börje Filipson and Jöns Filipson. The executing’s continued on the square multiple times (including Erik Puke the year of 1437).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:12pt;font-family:Cambria;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;"&gt;The council hall was the city’s most important building until 1732. It was where the city’s councilors met and made the decisions for the whole city.  Because the leading men and traders lived there it also became the city’s trade and financial center until the National bank was built at Järntorget (‘’The Iron Square’’) in 1682.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
 &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"&gt;&lt;img alt src="https://img.geocaching.com/cache/large/0372d808-be5c-416d-aae9-67ed1a696c64.jpg" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:12pt;font-family:Cambria;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;"&gt;In 1776 the new Börshus (‘’Stock Exchange House’’) was built in the north end of the square (see picture above from 1896) where the council hall previously was. The architects Johan Eberhard Carlberg and Erik Palmstedt designed the building. It was a commodity exchange with mostly iron, copper, silver and gold.  Since the year 1786 it is the Svenska Akademin (‘’Swedish Academy’’ who for instance gives out the Nobel price in litterateur) residence on the upper floor. It has an inscription that says ‘’Svenska Akademin’’ on the front of the building,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="font-size:12pt;font-family:Cambria;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;"&gt;over the window on the second floor.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
 &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:16pt;font-family:Cambria;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;"&gt;The Bloodbath&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"&gt;&lt;img alt src="https://img.geocaching.com/cache/large/18d7bf89-abea-48ff-8bad-958b52546ad7.jpg" style="width:500px;height:223px;" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:12pt;font-family:Cambria;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;"&gt;It was the year 1520 in September that the union king Kristian II successfully got through the town gate in to Stockholm with his foreign soldiers. He got crowned King of Sweden in November, it took place in the Storkyrkan (‘’The Big Church’’).  After the crowning there was suppose to be a celebration for three days. The 7&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:7.2pt;font-family:Cambria;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;vertical-align:super;white-space:pre-wrap;"&gt;th&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="font-size:12pt;font-family:Cambria;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;"&gt;of November they celebrated but the 8&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:7.2pt;font-family:Cambria;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;vertical-align:super;white-space:pre-wrap;"&gt;th&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="font-size:12pt;font-family:Cambria;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;"&gt;Kristian II accuse a number of Swedish people for treason and it ended in a blood bath. 82 people were beheaded in the northwest corner of the square, by the alley Trångsund.  Another 10 people was also hanged, but not on the square. It was said that the blood floated alongside Kåkbrinken and towards Väterlånggatan further down to the lake Mälaren.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:16pt;font-family:Cambria;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;"&gt;The Pump&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:16pt;font-family:Cambria;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;"&gt;&lt;img alt src="https://img.geocaching.com/cache/large/e4fa502c-bfb1-4f29-8056-da1b483a0bcf.jpg" /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:12pt;font-family:Cambria;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;"&gt;On The Big Square there is a pump with drinkable water.  Today it is connected to the normal water supply that goes to the households as well.  The pump has been there since the Middle Age, it was one of the town’s first fresh water sources. But not this particular well, it was rebuilt the year of 1778 designed by Erik Palmstedt.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
 &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:16pt;font-family:Cambria;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;"&gt;Cannonball&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:12pt;font-family:Cambria;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;"&gt;There is a cannonball on The Big Square or rather on the end of the house on the south side of the square, towards Skomakargatan. It has been there for hundreds of years and is said to have come from when Gustav Vasa occupied the city and drove away Kristian II. It was then when Sweden left the hated union and once again became a free country with our own king and government.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:12pt;font-family:Cambria;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;"&gt;Maybe that is not the whole truth but the legend. This is what truly happened: The furniture dealer Fredrik Christian Hans Grevesmuhl had in 1795 a ‘’Gustavianskt’’ house on the corner of the square and had the cannonball built in on purpose.  That was approximately 250 years after the event actually occurred. His motive was to create a monument of Gustav Vasa’s siege that forced Kristian II to surrender and led to a free Sweden from the union time, and a kind of revenge for the blood bath he caused in 1520. Because of the cannonball the house sometimes is called Rövarkulan (‘’Rober ball’’) or just Huset kulan (‘’House ball’’).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
 &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:12pt;font-family:Cambria;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;"&gt;Last but not least, to be able to log this Virtual Cache as Found you have to go to the coordinates and take a photo of you or your GPS with the canonball on the house visible in the background and post it together with your log. If you log it without the requirements it will be deleted.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt; &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt; &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Virtual Reward - 2017/2018&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This Virtual Cache is part of a limited release of Virtuals created between August 24, 2017 and August 24, 2018. Only 4,000 cache owners were given the opportunity to hide a Virtual Cache. Learn more about Virtual Rewards on the &lt;a href="https://www.geocaching.com/blog/2017/08/virtual-rewards/"&gt;Geocaching Blog&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

