Tack för den.😊</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1381347694"><groundspeak:date>2026-08-28T12:00:00</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="9313472">Elwija</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">TFTC</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="881747947"><groundspeak:date>2019-09-12T12:00:00</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="24157615">mikkokalevi</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Roadtrip matkalla itärajaa pitkin pohjoiseen  ja käsivarren kautta takaisin etelään TPTH:n kanssa samalla kuntia värittäen... lokattu omilla nimimerkeillä...  Kiitos kätköstä </groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log></groundspeak:logs></groundspeak:cache></wpt><wpt lat="59.3157" lon="18.0974"><time>2011-07-08T00:00:00</time><name>GC2ZNDW</name><desc>Welcome to Stockholm - Tervetuloa Tukholmaan! by Möjagumman</desc><url>https://www.geocaching.com/geocache/GC2ZNDW</url><urlname>Welcome to Stockholm - Tervetuloa Tukholmaan!</urlname><sym>Geocache Found</sym><type>Geocache|Traditional Cache</type><groundspeak:cache id="2350263" available="true" archived="false"><groundspeak:name>Welcome to Stockholm - Tervetuloa Tukholmaan!</groundspeak:name><groundspeak:placed_by>Möjagumman</groundspeak:placed_by><groundspeak:owner id="2378037">Möjagumman</groundspeak:owner><groundspeak:type>Traditional Cache</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:container>Small</groundspeak:container><groundspeak:attributes><groundspeak:attribute id="42" inc="1">Needs maintenance</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="24" inc="1">Wheelchair accessible</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="6" inc="1">Recommended for kids</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="41" inc="1">Stroller accessible</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="13" inc="1">Available 24/7</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="25" inc="1">Parking nearby</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="40" inc="1">Stealth required</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="26" inc="1">Public transportation nearby</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="15" inc="1">Available in winter</groundspeak:attribute></groundspeak:attributes><groundspeak:difficulty>2</groundspeak:difficulty><groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain><groundspeak:country>Sweden</groundspeak:country><groundspeak:state>Stockholm</groundspeak:state><groundspeak:short_description /><groundspeak:long_description>When arriving in Stockholm by a cruise ship one of the most frequent harbours is Masthamnen (Mast Port) at the island Södermalm. A shipbuilding yard was established here in 1687 and was called The South Shipyard or The Big Shipyard. The activity ceased in 1930. Nowadays big cruising ships from Åland/Finland and other countries land here. From the harbour you can have a nice walk along the quay to the Old Town and the city. 

I really hope you will enjoy your stay in Stockholm and that you will find many of the caches that can be found here!</groundspeak:long_description><groundspeak:encoded_hints /><groundspeak:logs><groundspeak:log id="1381682765"><groundspeak:date>2026-08-30T12:33:55</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="17938982">lovisastaflin</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Tftc</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1381661171"><groundspeak:date>2026-08-30T12:00:00</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="14352783">KiddoFreak</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Second Day in Stockholm we walk to the old town. We found a lot of very wonderful buildings and location. Very good Cache and our last found.

Favo in

Best regrads from Bamberg-Germany</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1381659517"><groundspeak:date>2026-08-30T10:59:14</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="1261077">Panda99</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Vi besökte Stockholm idag med AidaMar. Under en kort morgonpromenad hittade vi några cacher. Stort tack för att ni visade oss dem.</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1381510875"><groundspeak:date>2026-08-29T16:59:25</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="2202177">Taldran</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Found it on our Trip through the baltic sea :) TFTC </groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1381564064"><groundspeak:date>2026-08-29T12:00:00</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="18235912">ra65ma91la95ja68</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Schnell gefunden, an einem sehr regenreichen Tag.
Grüße von der AIDAmar</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="835489416"><groundspeak:date>2019-03-23T13:04:49</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Unknown</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="24157615">mikkokalevi</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Tämä kätköilijä ilmoitti, että purkki on vahingoittunut.</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="835489409"><groundspeak:date>2019-03-23T12:00:00</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="24157615">mikkokalevi</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Found easily. Logbook wet. Tv out</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log></groundspeak:logs></groundspeak:cache></wpt><wpt lat="59.316883" lon="18.088133"><time>2008-06-18T00:00:00</time><name>GC1DBGG</name><desc>OTTT #7 – Fjällgatan by Trang</desc><url>https://www.geocaching.com/geocache/GC1DBGG</url><urlname>OTTT #7 – Fjällgatan</urlname><sym>Geocache Found</sym><type>Geocache|Traditional Cache</type><groundspeak:cache id="910767" available="true" archived="false"><groundspeak:name>OTTT #7 – Fjällgatan</groundspeak:name><groundspeak:placed_by>Trang</groundspeak:placed_by><groundspeak:owner id="886479">Trang</groundspeak:owner><groundspeak:type>Traditional Cache</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:container>Micro</groundspeak:container><groundspeak:attributes><groundspeak:attribute id="8" inc="1">Scenic view</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="13" inc="1">Available 24/7</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="7" inc="1">Takes less than one hour</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="40" inc="1">Stealth required</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="30" inc="1">Picnic tables nearby</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="26" inc="1">Public transportation nearby</groundspeak:attribute></groundspeak:attributes><groundspeak:difficulty>2</groundspeak:difficulty><groundspeak:terrain>1.5</groundspeak:terrain><groundspeak:country>Sweden</groundspeak:country><groundspeak:state>Stockholm</groundspeak:state><groundspeak:short_description /><groundspeak:long_description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="http://img.geocaching.com/cache/39fecc9b-7c20-48df-8a86-e3be3efe2e86.jpg" /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;

&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;i&gt;Usually when geocaching, you get to see new and interesting
places you probably would not have seen otherwise, and that is one
of the great things about this hobby. But what if you are short of
time when visiting a new town, and want to see the main tourist
attractions and do some geocaching as well?&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;i&gt;In Stockholm the &lt;b&gt;On the Tourist Trail&lt;/b&gt; (OTTT) –
series of caches could be the answer. These seven caches (plus one
bonus mystery) are all hidden next to main tourist attractions, all
on the Top-ten list of most visited places in town. The OTTT-caches
are all traditionals, the stashes are 0,4 l ”Lock and
Lock”-boxes with enough room for small trading items, and
they should not be too hard to find.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;i&gt;The caches are: &lt;a href="http://www.geocaching.com/seek/cache_details.aspx?guid=b1629f16-9f46-49c0-84f9-585d8dbb9b27"&gt;
&lt;b&gt;OTTT #1&lt;/b&gt; – City Hall&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="http://www.geocaching.com/seek/cache_details.aspx?guid=611b097b-e43c-46ee-aae0-32c5b837f720"&gt;
&lt;b&gt;OTTT #2&lt;/b&gt; – Changing of the Guard&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="http://www.geocaching.com/seek/cache_details.aspx?guid=ceedb2d1-e325-4d00-8125-baefed5f6792"&gt;
&lt;b&gt;OTTT #3&lt;/b&gt; – Sightseeing&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="http://www.geocaching.com/seek/cache_details.aspx?guid=891e3d60-a783-4f92-8a4e-ae3f306fcaa3"&gt;
&lt;b&gt;OTTT #4&lt;/b&gt; – Museum of Modern Art&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="http://www.geocaching.com/seek/cache_details.aspx?guid=1d8f6fe3-9062-4c69-8c73-b5fa16009ce5"&gt;
&lt;b&gt;OTTT #5&lt;/b&gt; – Vasa&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="http://www.geocaching.com/seek/cache_details.aspx?guid=23afd7aa-066a-44b2-ada2-43f3f0c85d22"&gt;
&lt;b&gt;OTTT #6&lt;/b&gt; – Skansen&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/i&gt;, &lt;i&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.geocaching.com/seek/cache_details.aspx?guid=2b8b0a96-c3cf-417c-85d6-8c162c43ec5f"&gt;
&lt;b&gt;OTTT #7&lt;/b&gt; – Fjällgatan&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;and the bonus
mystery&lt;/i&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.geocaching.com/seek/cache_details.aspx?guid=8cdc612a-0248-4bce-a6d8-71f209770087"&gt;&lt;b&gt;OTTT
#8&lt;/b&gt; – Bulls Eye&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/i&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;img src="http://img.geocaching.com/cache/cd12d7c2-bab3-42b8-9170-5f0bade4bd4a.jpg" /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font size="+2"&gt;Fjällgatan&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
 &lt;br /&gt;
From here you have one of the best views of Stockholm, don't miss
to bring your camera. If life gets to busy out On the Tourist
Trail, you can rest for a while in the quiet little garden at N 59°
19.028, E 018° 05.162. Or, during summer, have a cup of coffe at
the outdoor café nearby.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;Note:&lt;/b&gt; The satellite reception is not to good at this
spot, so the coordinates are probably slightly off within a few
meters. The cache has been muggled several times, so please be very
stealthy while searching, and hide the box well after logging,
thanks.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
In the cache was from start:&lt;br /&gt;
Log book&lt;br /&gt;
Stash note&lt;br /&gt;
Bracelet&lt;br /&gt;
Necklace&lt;br /&gt;
Small car&lt;br /&gt;
Mobile phone stickers&lt;br /&gt;
Small FTF-prize&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
