TFTC f1nn</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1380113143"><groundspeak:date>2026-08-22T17:22:28</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="41494182">skyarnas</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">TYFTC!! Lätt och kul 😊</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="835474692"><groundspeak:date>2019-03-23T12:00:00</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="24157615">mikkokalevi</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Found nicely. Thanks for cache</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log></groundspeak:logs></groundspeak:cache></wpt><wpt lat="59.317217" lon="18.08615"><time>2007-07-09T00:00:00</time><name>GC148A8</name><desc>Sista Styverns Trappor/Last Farthing's Stairs by kerran&amp;lasse</desc><url>https://www.geocaching.com/geocache/GC148A8</url><urlname>Sista Styverns Trappor/Last Farthing's Stairs</urlname><sym>Geocache Found</sym><type>Geocache|Traditional Cache</type><groundspeak:cache id="639571" available="false" archived="true"><groundspeak:name>Sista Styverns Trappor/Last Farthing's Stairs</groundspeak:name><groundspeak:placed_by>kerran&amp;lasse</groundspeak:placed_by><groundspeak:owner id="941998">kerran&amp;lasse</groundspeak:owner><groundspeak:type>Traditional Cache</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:container>Micro</groundspeak:container><groundspeak:attributes><groundspeak:attribute id="42" inc="1">Needs maintenance</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="6" inc="1">Recommended for kids</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="1" inc="1">Dogs</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="8" inc="1">Scenic view</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="13" inc="1">Available 24/7</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="7" inc="1">Takes less than one hour</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="32" inc="1">Bicycles</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="15" inc="1">Available in winter</groundspeak:attribute></groundspeak:attributes><groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty><groundspeak:terrain>1.5</groundspeak:terrain><groundspeak:country>Sweden</groundspeak:country><groundspeak:state>Stockholm</groundspeak:state><groundspeak:short_description /><groundspeak:long_description>De ursprungliga Sista Styverns Trappor byggdes antagligen på 1600-talet. De var av trä och slingrade sig, smala och branta, från Stadsgården och upp på Stigberget,  bredvid andra liknande trappor. Sista Styvern var en av krogarna nere i Stadsgården och där tog man en sista sup innan man seglade ut – eller tog sig upp för trapporna. Stigberget kallades förr Galgberget och var en av Stockholms avrättningsplatser. Högst upp på berget fanns galgen och den syntes avskräckande över hela stan och var också inritad på dåtidens sjökort. Galgen hade ett fundament av sten och där ovanpå tre stenpelare med träbjälkar mellan sig och vid dem var repen fästade. Fullhängt var det när nio kroppar dinglade i galgen. Trapporna som är kvar idag går från Fjällgatan, som förr hette Galgbergsgatan, upp till Stigbergsgatan som i sin tur bödeln själv givit namn åt: Mikaelsgränd eller Mikaels Trappgränd.

---

The original Last Farthing’s Stairs were probably built in the 17th century. They were made of wood and winded, tiny and steep, from Stadsgården beside the water up to Stigberget, the mountain that also had the name of Gallows Mountain. They say that the gallows was fully-hanged when nine bodies were swinging. The gallows was seen all over Stockholm and was perhaps a deterrent landmark.</groundspeak:long_description><groundspeak:encoded_hints>(SWE) 12 steg upp
(ENG) 12 steps up
</groundspeak:encoded_hints><groundspeak:logs><groundspeak:log id="1106594768"><groundspeak:date>2022-06-27T10:02:59</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Archived</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="4037893">Toa Norik</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">#This cache has been archived by a Swedish reviewer#
 
